{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "41d61982",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Sub-reporte de causa en incendios forestales (FPA-FOD)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Seminario Final — Lic. en Ciencia de Datos, UNaB · Facundo Tarizzo**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hipótesis:** la ausencia de causa de ignición reportada (8,9% de los registros) no es\n",
    "aleatoria, sino que responde a factores administrativos (jurisdicción, período, agencia\n",
    "reportante) y no a características físicas del incendio. Si es así, debería ser predecible\n",
    "usando solo esas variables.\n",
    "\n",
    "*Trabajo en curso.*\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Carga de datos\n",
    "\n",
    "La base FPA-FOD viene en formato SQLite. Se carga la tabla `Fires` completa\n",
    "(1,88 millones de registros)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "455d704b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
    "\n",
    "import sqlite3\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from catboost import CatBoostClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (roc_auc_score, average_precision_score, precision_recall_curve,\n",
    "                              precision_score, recall_score, f1_score, confusion_matrix, roc_curve)\n",
    "\n",
    "RUTA_DB = '/content/drive/MyDrive/Tesis/FPA_FOD_20170508.sqlite'\n",
    "\n",
    "conn = sqlite3.connect(RUTA_DB)\n",
    "df = pd.read_sql(\"SELECT * FROM Fires;\", conn)\n",
    "conn.close()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Registros cargados: {len(df):,}\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(df['STAT_CAUSE_DESCR'].value_counts(dropna=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7fa279f1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 2. Variable objetivo\n",
    "\n",
    "Se construye `ES_MISSING`: 1 si el incendio no tiene causa reportada, 0 si la tiene."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "91ef8647",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df['ES_MISSING'] = (df['STAT_CAUSE_DESCR'] == 'Missing/Undefined').astype(int)\n",
    "missing = df[df['ES_MISSING'] == 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Total de registros:        {len(df):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Sin causa reportada:       {len(missing):,}  ({df['ES_MISSING'].mean()*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Con causa conocida:        {len(df) - len(missing):,}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "28e552b7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 3. Hallazgo 1 — Concentración geográfica-temporal\n",
    "\n",
    "Si el missing fuera aleatorio, debería repartirse parejo entre estados y años. El heatmap\n",
    "muestra lo contrario: hay bloques Estado-Año casi enteramente en blanco (reportan todo) o\n",
    "casi enteramente en negro (no reportan nada), con pocos casos intermedios."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1a4a859",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "total_por_estado_anio = df.groupby(['STATE', 'FIRE_YEAR']).size()\n",
    "missing_por_estado_anio = missing.groupby(['STATE', 'FIRE_YEAR']).size()\n",
    "pct_missing = (missing_por_estado_anio / total_por_estado_anio * 100).unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filtramos estados con volumen mínimo para no meter ruido\n",
    "vol_estado = df.groupby('STATE').size()\n",
    "estados_relevantes = vol_estado[vol_estado > 1000].index\n",
    "pct_missing = pct_missing.loc[pct_missing.index.intersection(estados_relevantes)]\n",
    "pct_missing = pct_missing.loc[pct_missing.mean(axis=1).sort_values(ascending=False).index]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(16, 12))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(pct_missing, cmap='Greys', vmin=0, vmax=100,\n",
    "            cbar_kws={'label': '% de incendios con causa no determinada'},\n",
    "            linewidths=0.3, linecolor='#f0f0f0', ax=ax)\n",
    "ax.set_title('Proporción de causa no determinada por Estado y Año (1992-2015)',\n",
    "             fontsize=14, fontweight='bold', loc='left')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Año'); ax.set_ylabel('Estado')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('heatmap_missingness.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d461540d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cuantificación: bloques Estado-Año con más del 80% de missing\n",
    "UMBRAL = 80\n",
    "\n",
    "pct_largo = pct_missing.stack().reset_index()\n",
    "pct_largo.columns = ['STATE', 'FIRE_YEAR', 'PCT_MISSING']\n",
    "estado_anio_alto = pct_largo[pct_largo['PCT_MISSING'] > UMBRAL]\n",
    "\n",
    "en_bloques = missing.merge(estado_anio_alto[['STATE','FIRE_YEAR']], on=['STATE','FIRE_YEAR'])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Combinaciones Estado-Año con >{UMBRAL}% de missing: {len(estado_anio_alto)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Concentran el {len(en_bloques)/len(missing)*100:.1f}% de todos los registros sin causa\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b909696e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 4. Hallazgo 2 — Patrón institucional\n",
    "\n",
    "`NWCG_REPORTING_AGENCY` identifica el tipo de organización que generó el reporte. Códigos\n",
    "según la documentación oficial del dataset (Short, 2017): FS = Forest Service,\n",
    "ST/C&L = Estado/Condado/Local, IA = Interagency Organization, BIA = Bureau of Indian\n",
    "Affairs, BLM = Bureau of Land Management, NPS = National Park Service, FWS = Fish &\n",
    "Wildlife Service."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9750260d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tabla_agencia = pd.crosstab(df['NWCG_REPORTING_AGENCY'], df['ES_MISSING'] == 1,\n",
    "                             normalize='index') * 100\n",
    "tabla_agencia.columns = ['% Causa conocida', '% Missing']\n",
    "tabla_agencia['n_registros'] = df['NWCG_REPORTING_AGENCY'].value_counts()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(tabla_agencia.sort_values('% Missing', ascending=False).round(2))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1f31a8b9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Las agencias con procesos de reporte estandarizados (FS) casi nunca omiten la causa;\n",
    "los reportes interagenciales (IA) la omiten casi siempre.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Advertencia de interpretación:** DOD (81 registros), BOR (14) y DOE (2) tienen muestras\n",
    "demasiado chicas como para generalizar sus tasas extremas. `ST/C&L`, con el 73% del volumen\n",
    "del dataset, es la que más aporta al total de faltantes en términos absolutos aunque su tasa\n",
    "sea moderada.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "## 5. Preparación del modelo\n",
    "\n",
    "**Validación temporal** (train 1992–2010 / test 2011–2015) en lugar de split aleatorio: con\n",
    "autocorrelación espacial y temporal, un split aleatorio deja en el conjunto de prueba casos\n",
    "casi idénticos a los de entrenamiento, inflando la performance (Roberts et al., 2017).\n",
    "\n",
    "Las **tasas históricas de missing** se calculan únicamente sobre el período de entrenamiento\n",
    "para evitar fuga de información hacia el período de prueba."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3ae6b912",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "features_base = ['FIRE_YEAR', 'DISCOVERY_DOY', 'LATITUDE', 'LONGITUDE',\n",
    "                 'STATE', 'OWNER_DESCR', 'NWCG_REPORTING_AGENCY', 'FIRE_SIZE']\n",
    "cat_features = ['STATE', 'OWNER_DESCR', 'NWCG_REPORTING_AGENCY']\n",
    "cat_idx = [features_base.index(c) for c in cat_features]\n",
    "\n",
    "train_full = df[df['FIRE_YEAR'] <= 2010].copy()\n",
    "test_full  = df[df['FIRE_YEAR'] >  2010].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Imputación simple de nulos\n",
    "for d in [train_full, test_full]:\n",
    "    for col in features_base:\n",
    "        if d[col].dtype == 'object':\n",
    "            d[col] = d[col].fillna('Desconocido')\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            d[col] = d[col].fillna(train_full[col].median())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Target encoding calculado SOLO sobre train\n",
    "tasa_estado         = train_full.groupby('STATE')['ES_MISSING'].mean()\n",
    "tasa_agencia        = train_full.groupby('NWCG_REPORTING_AGENCY')['ES_MISSING'].mean()\n",
    "tasa_estado_agencia = train_full.groupby(['STATE','NWCG_REPORTING_AGENCY'])['ES_MISSING'].mean()\n",
    "media_global        = train_full['ES_MISSING'].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "for d in [train_full, test_full]:\n",
    "    d['TASA_MISSING_ESTADO']  = d['STATE'].map(tasa_estado).fillna(media_global)\n",
    "    d['TASA_MISSING_AGENCIA'] = d['NWCG_REPORTING_AGENCY'].map(tasa_agencia).fillna(media_global)\n",
    "    d['TASA_MISSING_ESTADO_AGENCIA'] = (d.set_index(['STATE','NWCG_REPORTING_AGENCY'])\n",
    "                                          .index.map(tasa_estado_agencia))\n",
    "    d['TASA_MISSING_ESTADO_AGENCIA'] = d['TASA_MISSING_ESTADO_AGENCIA'].fillna(media_global)\n",
    "\n",
    "features_final = features_base + ['TASA_MISSING_ESTADO', 'TASA_MISSING_AGENCIA',\n",
    "                                   'TASA_MISSING_ESTADO_AGENCIA']\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train, y_train = train_full[features_final], train_full['ES_MISSING']\n",
    "X_test,  y_test  = test_full[features_final],  test_full['ES_MISSING']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Train: {len(train_full):,} registros ({train_full['FIRE_YEAR'].min()}-{train_full['FIRE_YEAR'].max()})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test:  {len(test_full):,} registros ({test_full['FIRE_YEAR'].min()}-{test_full['FIRE_YEAR'].max()})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Proporción de clase positiva en train: {y_train.mean():.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2201d0dd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 6. Modelo — CatBoost\n",
    "\n",
    "CatBoost maneja variables categóricas de forma nativa (sin one-hot encoding), lo cual es\n",
    "conveniente con `STATE` (49 categorías) y `NWCG_REPORTING_UNIT_ID`.\n",
    "\n",
    "`task_type='GPU'` requiere GPU activada en Colab (Entorno de ejecución → Cambiar tipo de\n",
    "entorno de ejecución). Sin GPU, quitar esa línea y `devices`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7ef0cf65",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "modelo_final = CatBoostClassifier(\n",
    "    iterations=500,\n",
    "    depth=5,\n",
    "    learning_rate=0.03,\n",
    "    l2_leaf_reg=5,\n",
    "    loss_function='Logloss',\n",
    "    task_type='GPU',\n",
    "    devices='0',\n",
    "    cat_features=cat_idx,\n",
    "    random_seed=42,\n",
    "    early_stopping_rounds=100,\n",
    "    use_best_model=True,\n",
    "    verbose=100\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "modelo_final.fit(X_train, y_train, eval_set=(X_test, y_test))\n",
    "proba = modelo_final.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2b6ac0ee",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 7. Evaluación\n",
    "\n",
    "Se prioriza **AUC-PR** sobre accuracy o AUC-ROC: con 8,9% de clase positiva, las métricas\n",
    "que promedian sobre todo el conjunto se ven infladas por lo fácil que resulta acertar en la\n",
    "clase mayoritaria."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c0f69837",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "auc_roc = roc_auc_score(y_test, proba)\n",
    "auc_pr  = average_precision_score(y_test, proba)\n",
    "azar    = y_test.mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=\"*55)\n",
    "print(\"MÉTRICAS — test 2011-2015\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*55)\n",
    "print(f\"AUC-ROC: {auc_roc:.4f}   (azar = 0.500)\")\n",
    "print(f\"AUC-PR:  {auc_pr:.4f}   (azar = {azar:.4f})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mejora sobre el azar: {auc_pr/azar:.1f}x\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fe5ae96c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Elección del umbral de decisión\n",
    "\n",
    "El umbral 0,5 por defecto es una mala elección con clases desbalanceadas. Se evalúan\n",
    "distintos puntos de corte."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0214719f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tabla_umbrales = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    {'umbral': u,\n",
    "     'precision': round(precision_score(y_test, (proba >= u).astype(int), zero_division=0), 3),\n",
    "     'recall':    round(recall_score(y_test, (proba >= u).astype(int), zero_division=0), 3),\n",
    "     'f1':        round(f1_score(y_test, (proba >= u).astype(int), zero_division=0), 3)}\n",
    "    for u in [0.10, 0.15, 0.20, 0.30, 0.40, 0.50]\n",
    "])\n",
    "print(tabla_umbrales.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "\n",
    "UMBRAL_ELEGIDO = 0.30\n",
    "print(f\"\\nMatriz de confusión (umbral {UMBRAL_ELEGIDO}):\")\n",
    "print(confusion_matrix(y_test, (proba >= UMBRAL_ELEGIDO).astype(int)))\n",
    "print(\"filas = real, columnas = predicho | [0] = causa reportada, [1] = causa faltante\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7674cf48",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "precision, recall, _ = precision_recall_curve(y_test, proba)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "ax.plot(recall, precision, color='#3b6fa0', linewidth=2, label=f'CatBoost (AUC-PR = {auc_pr:.3f})')\n",
    "ax.axhline(azar, color='gray', linestyle='--', linewidth=1, label=f'Azar ({azar:.3f})')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Recall'); ax.set_ylabel('Precisión')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Curva Precisión-Recall', fontweight='bold', loc='left')\n",
    "ax.legend(); ax.spines[['top','right']].set_visible(False)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('curva_precision_recall.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "124a03ce",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Importancia de variables\n",
    "\n",
    "Este es el resultado central para la hipótesis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1859c426",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "importancias = modelo_final.get_feature_importance(prettified=True)\n",
    "print(importancias.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 5))\n",
    "colores = ['#e07b39' if f in ['FIRE_SIZE', 'DISCOVERY_DOY'] else '#3b6fa0'\n",
    "           for f in importancias['Feature Id']]\n",
    "ax.barh(importancias['Feature Id'], importancias['Importances'], color=colores)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Importancia (%)')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Qué variables explican el sub-reporte de causa', fontweight='bold', loc='left')\n",
    "ax.invert_yaxis(); ax.spines[['top','right']].set_visible(False)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('importancia_variables.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b385f5d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "En naranja, las variables **físicas** del incendio: tamaño y estacionalidad. Ambas quedan\n",
    "en prácticamente cero. El sub-reporte no depende de cómo fue el incendio, sino de dónde,\n",
    "cuándo y quién lo reportó — que es exactamente lo que plantea la hipótesis.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "## 8. Comparación contra Random Forest\n",
    "\n",
    "Para no depender de un solo algoritmo. Random Forest no maneja categóricas nativas, así que\n",
    "requiere codificación ordinal previa."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4cf52ef1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import OrdinalEncoder\n",
    "\n",
    "encoder = OrdinalEncoder(handle_unknown='use_encoded_value', unknown_value=-1)\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train_rf, X_test_rf = X_train.copy(), X_test.copy()\n",
    "X_train_rf[cat_features] = encoder.fit_transform(X_train_rf[cat_features])\n",
    "X_test_rf[cat_features]  = encoder.transform(X_test_rf[cat_features])\n",
    "\n",
    "modelo_rf = RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=200, max_depth=8, class_weight='balanced',\n",
    "                                    random_state=42, n_jobs=-1)\n",
    "modelo_rf.fit(X_train_rf, y_train)\n",
    "proba_rf = modelo_rf.predict_proba(X_test_rf)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"{'Modelo':<16}{'AUC-ROC':>10}{'AUC-PR':>10}\")\n",
    "print(\"-\"*36)\n",
    "print(f\"{'CatBoost':<16}{auc_roc:>10.4f}{auc_pr:>10.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'Random Forest':<16}{roc_auc_score(y_test, proba_rf):>10.4f}{average_precision_score(y_test, proba_rf):>10.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f69a8172",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fpr_cb, tpr_cb, _ = roc_curve(y_test, proba)\n",
    "fpr_rf, tpr_rf, _ = roc_curve(y_test, proba_rf)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 6))\n",
    "ax.plot(fpr_cb, tpr_cb, color='#3b6fa0', linewidth=2, label=f'CatBoost (AUC = {auc_roc:.3f})')\n",
    "ax.plot(fpr_rf, tpr_rf, color='#e07b39', linewidth=2,\n",
    "        label=f'Random Forest (AUC = {roc_auc_score(y_test, proba_rf):.3f})')\n",
    "ax.plot([0,1], [0,1], color='gray', linestyle='--', linewidth=1)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Tasa de falsos positivos'); ax.set_ylabel('Tasa de verdaderos positivos')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Comparación de modelos — curva ROC', fontweight='bold', loc='left')\n",
    "ax.legend(); ax.spines[['top','right']].set_visible(False)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('comparacion_modelos.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7870c0d1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Random Forest ordena mejor el conjunto completo (AUC-ROC más alto), pero CatBoost es más\n",
    "preciso en la clase minoritaria (AUC-PR), que es la que interesa en este problema. Se adopta\n",
    "CatBoost como modelo principal por esa razón.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "## 9. Robustez ante distintos cortes temporales\n",
    "\n",
    "*(Pendiente de correr)* — verifica que el resultado no dependa del corte 2010/2011 elegido."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bf57d0c8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for corte in [2005, 2008, 2010, 2012]:\n",
    "    tr = df[df['FIRE_YEAR'] <= corte].copy()\n",
    "    te = df[df['FIRE_YEAR'] >  corte].copy()\n",
    "    if len(te) < 1000:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    for d in [tr, te]:\n",
    "        for col in features_base:\n",
    "            if d[col].dtype == 'object':\n",
    "                d[col] = d[col].fillna('Desconocido')\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                d[col] = d[col].fillna(tr[col].median())\n",
    "\n",
    "    t_e  = tr.groupby('STATE')['ES_MISSING'].mean()\n",
